WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:05.372
 Ron, Jesse, I'm renaming this
competition papa don't take no

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:09.575
mess because it's just the
patriarchs of the families

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:12.078
going at it in our final round
of this competition where

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:14.814
we're sending you back to
your home forges to recreate

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:22.855
this iconic weapon
from history, the Inigo

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.991
Montoya-inspired rapier.

00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:25.925
You know the guy.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:26.825
You killed my father.

00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:30.663
Prepare to forge, all right.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.764
Good luck bladesmiths.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.366
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.336
RON: I am almost
positive that they're

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:41.574
going to do some kind of a flex
test, so I'm choosing ADCR-V2.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:42.742
That should help with that.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.643
The hilt is one of the
more complex pieces here.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.380
I'm actually going to use
some really old wrought iron.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:49.682
One of the really nice
things about wrought iron

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.083
is that it's beautiful.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.185
My plan is to [inaudible]
so you can see

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:56.022
the lines around this thing.

00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:58.157
I'm working on my normalization.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.692
This is make or break.

00:00:59.758 --> 00:01:02.362
If it works well, I'm all set.

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:05.498
I grab hold of it with another
pair of tongs and go for it.

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:09.001
I am very pleased right now to
have, at the end of day one,

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:12.071
a quenched blade
ready for temper.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.173 line:7%
So far I'm on track.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.675 line:0%
JESSE: After coming
out of the temper,

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:19.045 line:0%
I noticed that there was just a
slight little yaw in the edge.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:22.849
[inaudible] take all of
that out and grind it today.

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:25.084
Next, I'm going to
move on to the hilt.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.619
I'm planning on
forging all the parts

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.788
for the hilt out of
an old wagon wheel

00:01:28.854 --> 00:01:31.224
that my grandfather used to own.

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:40.066
So I'm flipping it over, and
I ended up getting a crack.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.902
Got a small crack that's
developed in the piece

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.737
that I was forging
for my pommel.

00:01:44.803 --> 00:01:47.440
I'm going to try to see if I
can get that crack out of it.

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:55.915
Luckily took one more
good, hot welded heat,

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:58.284
and we're good to go.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.187
I feel better today
than I did on day one.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.790
End of day two, I'm ready
to go put my feet up.

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:07.927 line:0%
RON: Well, my goal
is to actually

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:09.395 line:7%
get done with the blade today.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.465
It leaves me two days to work
on all of the embellishments.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:15.067
I may get into doing some
of the hilt work today.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.736
I want to see how it
goes with the grinding.

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:20.739
If I over grind, I could
completely destroy the blade.

00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:23.909
There's a reason that it
took Inigo Montoya's father

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:25.178
a year to make this sword.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:27.247
There are so many
pieces to this.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:31.283 line:0%
But for Jessica, I'm going to
get this done in four days.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.520
JESSE: I got a little bit
behind where I would like to be.

00:02:34.586 --> 00:02:36.389
I'm going to try to
make up a little time.

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:38.891
I'm going to go ahead and
forge out my knuckle-bow,

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:44.096
and hopefully by lunchtime when
you start fabricating the hilt.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:46.498
This hilt's been
pretty demanding.

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:48.902
There's about six
different pieces here.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.838
We spent a lot of time trying
to make sure everything

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.806
was dialed in.

00:02:53.872 --> 00:02:58.077
End of day three, my hilt all
came together pretty nicely.

00:02:58.143 --> 00:02:59.345
Just pulled it out of the etch.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:00.980
Everything looks good.

00:03:01.046 --> 00:03:02.849
Tomorrow will just
be fit and finish.

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:08.353 line:0%
RON: Last day, I have to
get done, well, everything.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.424
Now I can focus on getting
that really complex

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.659
handle and hilt all together.

00:03:13.692 --> 00:03:15.327
I'm forging out these
bigger rings that

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:17.263
are on the side of the hand.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.731
That's eventually
going to become

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.800
this really complex basket.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.335
Not perfect, but for
day four, I'll take it.

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:25.138
Regardless of the
outcome on this thing,

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.605
I've had a blast making this.

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:29.575
Win, lose, or draw, it's
just been so much fun.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:30.476
 Good job.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:32.178
 Thank you.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:35.180
 All right, bladesmiths,
my name is Douglas Marcaida.

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:37.149
I will kill the dummies.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.584
They are prepared to die.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:41.453
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapons will do,

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:42.821
I will take your
rapiers and deliver

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:45.458
some thrusts and slashes
on this ballistics dummy.

00:03:45.524 --> 00:03:47.025
Ron, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:47.793
 Absolutely.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.128
 Let's do it.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:53.333
[music playing]

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:29.301
 All right, Ron, let's
talk about your rapier here.

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:31.337
It is a little bit
on the heavier side,

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:32.605
but it's wieldable.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:37.176
And with a nice swish of
a slash, it cuts deeply.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:39.778
Overall, sir, your
rapier, it will kill.

00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:40.579
Good job.

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:41.447
 Thank you

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:42.315
 All right, Jesse,
it's your turn.

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.282
You ready, sir?

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:44.083
 Yes, sir.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.117
 Let's do this.

00:04:45.183 --> 00:04:46.852
JESSE: I'm extremely nervous.

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:49.522
I immediately start
questioning my heat treat.

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:53.326
And, you know, just a million
things go through your head.

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:56.963
[music playing]

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:23.255
 All right, Jesse, let's
talk about your blade here.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:25.258
It's about the same weight.

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:27.260
The thrusts penetrate
all the way.

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:30.129
And slash, well, deep cuts.

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:33.132
Overall, sir, your
blade will kill.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.099
 Thank you, sir.

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:34.801
It's what I came to hear.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:40.272
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test.

00:05:40.305 --> 00:05:42.441
And yes, I am going to
torture your blades.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.276
Ron, you're up first.

00:05:44.309 --> 00:05:45.078
 All right.

00:05:55.954 --> 00:05:59.425
 If you haven't guessed
already, it's a flex test.

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:02.295
RON: I'm feeling a little
nervous coming into this test.

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:04.697
If I left any uneven
spots, that could impact

00:06:04.763 --> 00:06:06.499
the flexibility of that blade.

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:33.626
 Good job, man.

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:34.827
Good job.

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:39.231
 OK, Ron, that's a brutal
test, and you did really well.

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:40.766
If you look at
your blade, there's

00:06:40.832 --> 00:06:45.871
the slightest of bend in one
direction, barely noticeable.

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:49.508
The dimensions of the
guard are spot on,

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:51.810
and it's definitely
a strong blade.

00:06:51.877 --> 00:06:52.511
Nicely done.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:53.478
 Thank you very much.

00:06:53.545 --> 00:06:54.613
 Jesse, you ready for this?

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.048
 About as nervous
as a long-tailed

00:06:56.114 --> 00:06:58.283
cat in a room full of
rocking chairs, but go ahead.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:02.522
 [laughs]

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:32.618
First things, Jesse, the
guard's at the proper scale.

00:07:32.685 --> 00:07:33.819
Really nicely done.

00:07:33.885 --> 00:07:36.955
The issue is you've
picked a bit of a bend.

00:07:37.022 --> 00:07:40.292
Still a completely
functional, usable blade.

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:41.126
Well done.

00:07:41.193 --> 00:07:41.961
 Thank you.

00:07:44.397 --> 00:07:46.799
 Bladesmiths, this
is the sharpness test.

00:07:46.832 --> 00:07:48.567
This is all about how
sharp your blade is

00:07:48.633 --> 00:07:51.169
and what it does to this dummy.

00:07:51.236 --> 00:07:52.137
Ron, you're up first.

00:07:52.204 --> 00:07:52.971
You ready for this?

00:07:53.038 --> 00:07:53.606
 Yes, sir.

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:56.108
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:07:56.175 --> 00:08:00.012
[music playing]

00:08:08.587 --> 00:08:10.490
All right, Ron, let's
talk about your edge here.

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:14.327
This cut through the clothing
and right into the foam.

00:08:14.393 --> 00:08:16.528
And, of course, when
thrusting, it goes deep.

00:08:16.595 --> 00:08:19.531
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:08:19.598 --> 00:08:20.666
 Thank you.

00:08:20.733 --> 00:08:21.700
 All right, Jesse,
it's your turn, sir.

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:22.668
You ready?
- Yes, sir.

00:08:22.735 --> 00:08:25.471
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:08:25.538 --> 00:08:29.041
[music playing]

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:40.319
 All right, Jesse,
I can still see

00:08:40.386 --> 00:08:41.720
the little bend it
took at the tip,

00:08:41.786 --> 00:08:44.590
but the edges are razor sharp.

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:47.025
On the thrust, it goes deep.

00:08:47.092 --> 00:08:47.893
It will cut.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.561
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:51.764
 Ron, Jesse, you
guys have turned

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:54.367
in some really quality blades.

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:56.001
This is a difficult
decision for us to make,

00:08:56.068 --> 00:09:04.076
and our "Forged in
Fire" champion is Ron.

00:09:04.143 --> 00:09:05.077
Congratulations.

00:09:05.144 --> 00:09:07.380
You are the new "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:07.446 --> 00:09:10.349
Jesse, please
surrender your blade.

00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:11.650 line:0%
JESSE: Not being
the "Forged in Fire"

00:09:11.717 --> 00:09:14.020 line:0%
champion is kind of not
what I was looking for,

00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:16.622 line:0%
but I lost to a
heck of a competitor

00:09:16.689 --> 00:09:18.156 line:0%
and a heck of a blade.
- Well done.

00:09:18.223 --> 00:09:19.124
 Thank you.

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:20.492
I'm very proud of the
blade I turned in,

00:09:20.559 --> 00:09:22.295
but if I made this
blade again, I

00:09:22.328 --> 00:09:24.429
would have took a little
more time on my heat treat,

00:09:24.496 --> 00:09:26.098
made sure I had it perfect.

00:09:26.165 --> 00:09:29.701
Being able to start this journey
with my son was pretty awesome.

00:09:29.768 --> 00:09:32.371
And I may not be the
"Forged in Fire" champion,

00:09:32.438 --> 00:09:34.907
but I think I represented
my family well.

00:09:37.543 --> 00:09:38.844
 Ron, congratulations.

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:40.879
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:40.946 --> 00:09:43.148
You've led your family
to this position,

00:09:43.215 --> 00:09:47.053
and you'll be taking
home a check for $10,000.

00:09:47.119 --> 00:09:48.287
Good job, brother.

00:09:48.353 --> 00:09:49.989
RON: From beginning to end, this
has been a great experience.

00:09:50.056 --> 00:09:52.658
So the Hardman house is
getting a "Forged in Fire"

00:09:52.692 --> 00:09:54.994
championship.

